Z||000003||Greg Piet||09-18-2000||09:06 PM||||If I went to go buy a Fiero with the interior in decent shape, and I saw a sticker put on the visor, my first thought would be "Now why did some BLEEP have to go and do that!"  And then I would just be miffed because that would be a visor I would have to replace because in the 100 degree heat of Vegas (150 degree heat with the windows rolled up)the glue would impregnate into the cloth. I would be pretty miffed!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||09-18-2000||10:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Greg Piet:<BR><B>If I went to go buy a Fiero with the interior in decent shape, and I saw a sticker put on the visor, my first thought would be "Now why did some BLEEP have to go and do that!"  And then I would just be miffed because that would be a visor I would have to replace because in the 100 degree heat of Vegas (150 degree heat with the windows rolled up)the glue would impregnate into the cloth. I would be pretty miffed!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Theres no way I would put one on a "nice interior car" On nice ones I just drop a card under the seat.<BR><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">       <B>1985 Sport Coupe - Coming Soon 1987 SE</B><P><BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||14
